            <ArticleTitle>Fire in the Operating Room During Hypospadias Repair.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-25</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.eucr.2017.08.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fire in the operating room (OR) is a very distressful and shocking occurrence with potential dramatic consequences. Despite safety rules and rigorous recommendations, such unintentional events do occur every so often. Notably, the vast majority of cases have been reported in the adult population, with very few pediatric cases described to date. Herein, we report on a 16-month-old boy undergoing reconstructive surgery for penoscrotal hypospadias, who experienced an OR fire most likely related to the use of alcohol-based solution ignited by monopolar electrocautery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
